{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "WetDepLS",
    "description": "WRF-Chem's large-scale (grid-scale) wet deposition of every scavenged species over one column, `wetdep_ls` in chem/module_wetdep_ls.F (WRF v4.8.0), the scheme `wetscav_onoff < 0` selects. It is the only wet-scavenging path reachable with this project's chem_opt = 170 physics suite (WSM6 + New Tiedtke): `wetscav_onoff = 1` is fatal for chem_opt 170 and for mp_physics 6 in chemics_init, and convective-transport scavenging (`chem_conv_tr`, `conv_tr_wetscav`) needs a Grell-family cumulus scheme (FORTRAN_BUGS.md N115; that path also carries two defects of its own, B23 and B24). The species loop is a mapping, not physics -- the scheme treats every species alike apart from its efficiency `alpha` and the burden gate -- so it is written as a species axis `spc` (NSPEC long) over which the column fields `c`, `removal`, `c_out` and `dc_dt` and the per-species `alpha`, `burden` and `active` are shaped, while the column inputs (qc, rho, w, ze, rain) and everything built only from them (the cloud-water integral, `frc`, `f`) are shared. The consumer puts on that axis the species the scheme scavenges: first the NGAS gases it scavenges at alpha = 1 (gas-phase sulfuric acid `sulf` for chem_opt = 170), then every aerosol species of the mechanism (nv > numgas: MOSAIC's mass, number AND water of all eight bins, 168 for chem_opt = 170, at alpha = 0.5) -- NSPEC = 169, NGAS = 1. Every other gas is untouched. (Until 2026-11-12 the component took ONE species and the consumer mounted it once per species; a coupling over all 169 would then have needed 169 generated mounts, since esm has no mount-per-element and §10.5 lifting applies to 0-D systems only.)\n\nThe scheme. With R = rain/dt the step's grid-scale rain rate (WRF's `rainncv`, mm per step), it forms the column-integrated upward cloud-water flux C = integral of max(0, qc rho w) dz, and a conversion factor frc = clamp(R/C, 1e-6, 0.005), the fraction of that flux that falls as rain. Each layer then loses alpha f/(1+f) of the species, with f = frc rho dz w, the scavenged value floored at 1e-16. The tendency a consumer integrating the column must add is the operator-split increment over the step, `dc_dt = (c_out - c)/dt` (CLAUDE.md, operator-split schemes): the Fortran is an in-place update with no rate inside it, and its removal fraction f/(1+f) is the implicit-Euler form of a first-order loss at rate f/dt, so the increment converges to that loss as the step shrinks.\n\nWhat the scheme does that its comments do not say, all reproduced here. (1) The removal argument f is DIMENSIONALLY INCONSISTENT: frc carries 1/m, so f is a mass flux in kg m-2 s-1 that the Fortran adds to 1; the component divides by a unit flux `F_unit` to reproduce WRF's number (FORTRAN_BUGS.md B22). (2) `w` is WRF's `w_2(i,k,j)`, the vertical velocity on the BOTTOM face of layer k, not the layer's own; the surface face has w = 0, so the lowest layer is never scavenged. (3) The column sum runs over layers 1..NLEV-1 and the removal over 1..NLEV-2 (`k=1,kte-1` and `k=kts,kte-2` with kte = NLEV), so the top layer is excluded from the integral and the top two from the removal. (4) The burden gate is a plain level sum of c rho with no layer thickness, compared with a bare 1e-10 in whatever unit the species is carried in. (5) The removal needs qc > 0 in the layer but is not proportional to it: a layer with a trace of cloud water and a large updraught loses as much as a saturated one.\n\nInputs are consumer-supplied column fields (parameters with shape `lev`), following the column convention: real geometry `ze` from the consumer, the layer count a metaparameter.\n\nWhat the tests pin and what they cannot. Nine tests, one model step each, each on a two-species axis -- `sulf` (alpha = 1) and one aerosol species (alpha = 0.5) -- from a capture that switches the scheme on (data/eqwefic/chem170_scm/run_wetscav.sh: the reference column with wetscav_onoff = -1 and cu_physics = 0, steps 1300-1480 spanning a dry step, the onset at 2.7e-9 mm of rain, the 0.45 mm/step peak and the tail). Each asserts the per-species activation flags exactly; the removal fraction of every layer and species at 1e-9 of its largest value (it is a fraction, so one scale serves species whose units differ by 18 orders of magnitude; it is not taped by the kernel and is read from the replay as 1 - c_out/c where a layer was scavenged, never floored in this capture); the scavenged columns at 1e-9 of the largest value on the axis (an aerosol mass or number, which sets the scale of that check); and the tendency, likewise at 1e-9 of its largest magnitude, all against the real64 replay of the dumped inputs through chem/module_wetdep_ls.F compiled unchanged. The in-model real32 result agrees with that replay to 5.7e-8 of the column maximum over all 101 dumped steps and all 233 species. The full 169-species axis is exercised by couplings/wetdep_ls_column.esm. Quirk (3) is NOT exercised: extending the removal to layer NLEV-1 or the integral to layer NLEV fails nothing, because the top layers of this 20 km column never carry cloud water. The intermediates cw_column, frc and f are unasserted; they are pinned through the outputs they feed.",
    "authors": [
      "EqWeFiC"
    ],
    "created": "2026-11-11T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": [
      "wrf-chem",
      "wet-deposition",
      "wetdep_ls",
      "chem_opt-170",
      "column"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "WRF-Chem v4.8.0, chem/module_wetdep_ls.F (subroutine wetdep_ls), called from chem/chem_driver.F when wetscav_onoff < 0."
      }
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NLEV": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 59,
      "description": "Mass layers of the column, WRF kte (= e_vert - 1). Bound into the column grid at the import edge."
    },
    "NSPEC": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 2,
      "description": "Length of the species axis `spc`: the species this instance scavenges. 169 for chem_opt = 170 (sulf and MOSAIC's 168 aerosol species); 2 in this component's own tests (sulf and one aerosol species)."
    },
    "NGAS": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1,
      "description": "How many entries at the HEAD of the species axis are gases the scheme scavenges at par.alpha_sulf (sulf for chem_opt = 170; GOCART mechanisms would add their sea-salt bins). Every later entry is an aerosol species at par.alpha_aerosol."
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "spc": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NSPEC"
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "WetDepLS": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLEV": "NLEV"
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/integral_lev_whole.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLEV": "NLEV"
          }
        }
      ],
      "subsystems": {
        "par": {
          "ref": "./wetdep_ls_parameters.esm"
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "c": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "lev",
            "spc"
          ],
          "description": "The scavenged species, one column each, in their WRF chem units (ppmv for sulf; ug/kg for an aerosol mass, 1/kg for a number). The scheme's gates compare them with bare numbers in that unit, so they are declared dimensionless here and the gates carry the unit of the comparison."
        },
        "qc": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Cloud-water mixing ratio, moist(:,:,:,p_qc)."
        },
        "rho": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "default": 1.0,
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Air density as chem_driver passes it, `rho`."
        },
        "w": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Vertical velocity on the BOTTOM face of each layer, WRF `w_2(i,k,j)` as chem_driver copies it into `vvel` (k = 1 is the surface face, w = 0)."
        },
        "ze": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Heights of the layer faces; only their differences, the layer thicknesses (WRF dz8w), enter."
        },
        "rain": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/m^2",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Grid-scale rain over the step, WRF `rainncv` (mm per step, i.e. kg m-2)."
        },
        "dt": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 60.0,
          "description": "The model step the rain was accumulated over, `grid%dt`."
        },
        "alpha": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "spc"
          ],
          "description": "Scavenging efficiency of each species: par.alpha_sulf for the NGAS gases at the head of the axis, par.alpha_aerosol for every aerosol species."
        },
        "dz": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Layer thickness, WRF dz8w, from the grid template."
        },
        "z_sfc": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Bottom of the column, the integral's lower bound."
        },
        "z_top": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Top of the column, the integral's upper bound."
        },
        "rain_rate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/(m^2*s)",
          "description": "Grid-scale rain rate, `rain_clw = rain/dt`."
        },
        "cw_flux": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/(m^2*s)",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Upward cloud-water flux density of each layer, max(0, qc rho w), on the layers the column integral covers (1..NLEV-1) and zero on the top layer."
        },
        "cw_column": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/(m*s)",
          "description": "Column-integrated upward cloud-water flux, `var_sum_clw`."
        },
        "burden": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "description": "Level sum of c rho over layers 1..NLEV-1 for each species, `var_sum` (no layer thickness: a gate, not a burden in the physical sense).",
          "shape": [
            "spc"
          ]
        },
        "active": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 when the column scavenges this species at all -- rain, the species' burden and the cloud-water flux each above their gate -- else 0.",
          "shape": [
            "spc"
          ]
        },
        "frc": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/m",
          "description": "Conversion factor, rain rate over cloud-water flux clamped into [frc_min, frc_max], where rain and the cloud-water flux are both above their gates; else 0. The Fortran forms it inside the species loop under the burden gate as well, but its value does not depend on the species, and the burden gate is applied to the removal through `active`."
        },
        "f": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Per-layer removal argument max(0, frc rho dz w), divided by par.F_unit (see the model description). Shared by every species."
        },
        "removal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev",
            "spc"
          ],
          "description": "Fraction of each species each layer loses this step, alpha f/(1+f) where the layer is scavenged (species active, layer 1..NLEV-2, c above threshold, qc > 0), else 0."
        },
        "c_out": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev",
            "spc"
          ],
          "description": "Each species after the step's wet deposition, floored at par.c_threshold where scavenged."
        },
        "dc_dt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/s",
          "shape": [
            "lev",
            "spc"
          ],
          "description": "The operator-split tendency (c_out - c)/dt a consumer integrating the column adds."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "dz",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "column_cell_thickness",
            "bindings": {
